# Raiding Schemes ("Each noncreature spell you cast has conspire") and Silverquill, the Disputant ("Each instant and sorcery spell
# you cast has casualty 1") together give Lightning Bolt two optional costs (CR 601.2b, 702.78a, 702.153a). Bot1 pays both on turn 7:
# conspire taps the Goblin Champion and the Cacophony Scamp, casualty sacrifices the Scamp - a creature tapped as one cost is
# sacrificed as another, paid in any order (CR 601.2h) - and each ability's trigger copies the Bolt for its own cost. The Bolt hits
# Bot2 and the copies Bot1 (twice). Silverquill stays; the Scamp dies and its death trigger deals 1 to Bot2: Bot2 20-3-1 = 16, Bot1 14. The copies are no cards.

